        "turn": 160,
        "summary": "The output got cut off again. I see Rio, Curitiba, S\u00e3o Paulo, and Salvador is cut off. Let me check if there's a 5th city. The overview says 5 cities. Let me try to see what Salvador and the 5th city are doing.\n\nActually, looking at the data, I can see the cities are:\n1. Rio de Janeiro (id: 65536) - building Crossbowman\n2. Curitiba (id: 131073) - finishing Granary (1 turn)\n3. S\u00e3o Paulo (id: 196610) - building Granary (3 turns)\n4. Salvador - cut off\n5. ? - unknown\n\nLet me focus on what I can do. The Builders should repair the pillaged farms in Rio next turn. Let me also consider setting production for Curitiba once the Granary is done. But since it's only 1 turn left, it will complete this turn.\n\nLet me also check if I should set research or production for any other city. I'm researching Gunpowder which is appropriate.\n\nFor now, my main actions are done:\n1. Responded to diplomacy with Korea positively\n2. Moved both Builders to repair Rio's pillaged farms\n3. No pending trades to respond to\n\nLet me verify the deal status - I accepted deal-000002 where I need to keep military units 3 tiles away from Player 3. The favor is due turn 163, and payment (50 gold) is not due yet (on_delivery). I should make sure my military units stay away from Player 3's territory.\n\nI think I'm done for this turn. Let me provide a summary.\n\n---\n\n**Summary for Turn 160:**\n- Responded POSITIVELY to Korea's diplomacy session\n- Moved both Builders to Rio de Janeiro area to repair 5 pillaged farms\n- Curitiba's Granary will complete this turn (1 turn left)\n- Maintaining deal with Player 3: keeping military units 3+ tiles from their lands (favor due turn 163, 50 gold payment pending on delivery)\n- Continuing research on Gunpowder\n- Rio continues building Crossbowman (6 turns), S\u00e3o Paulo building Granary (3 turns)",
